              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Richie, petitioner argues that the Wagner Act allows a quorum of two members on a three\u2011member board, citing legislative history and past practice."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            },
            {
              "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), according to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), petitioner contends that the board\u2019s delegation to a three\u2011member panel remains effective even after a member departs, relying on the principle that delegated authority survives loss of the principal."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), according to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), petitioner points to historical evidence that the board has decided over 460 cases with only two members, indicating that such practice is permissible."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Katyal)",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-267f3f47bf91-0002-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 47,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), according to Petitioner (Mr. Katyal), petitioner argues that Congress was aware of the board operating with two members and that the board chose to maintain a three\u2011member panel rather than shut down."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "267f3f47bf9186b0f16d8040b9a65543734b13bbe9eeab9fecc2f55946cc23d9",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-267f3f47bf91-0001-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 31,
                "start": 31
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Katyal, petitioner emphasizes the quorum provision\u2019s language that \u201cquorum\u201d means a number sufficient to transact business, supporting the view that two members suffice after delegation."
        }
      ],
